Implement user story SKY-002-test: Test Skyscanner API client module

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch — no real network calls. Cover constructor validation, auth header, HTTP error handling, parse errors, mock mode, network errors, and input validation.

## Acceptance Criteria
- All tests mock the global fetch; no real network calls are made in any test
- Tests verify SkyscannerClient constructor: throws on missing apiKey and RAPIDAPI_KEY, uses constructor apiKey over env var, and apiKey is not publicly accessible on instances
- Tests verify searchFlights sends the apiKey as the correct RapidAPI authentication header and uses only the global fetch API
- Tests verify 4xx/5xx responses reject with an Error containing the status code and not containing the apiKey value
- Tests verify malformed response bodies reject with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- Tests verify MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns deterministic fixture without fetch invocation; other values (unset, empty, 'false', etc.) perform real fetch; real failures are never silently replaced with mock data
- Tests verify network-level fetch errors (DNS failure, connection refused) surface as rejections, not silent empty/fixture returns
- Tests verify empty-string origin, destination, or date rejects with a descriptive validation Error before any network request is made


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient is exported from './skyscanner/client' path
- Constructor signature: constructor(opts: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'SkyscannerClient requires an apiKey (constructor option or RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable)' when no apiKey provided via opts or RAPIDAPI_KEY env var
- Constructor prefers opts.apiKey over process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY when both provided and opts.apiKey is non-empty string
- apiKey is stored in private field #apiKey - not accessible via public property
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- searchFlights validation error for empty origin: 'searchFlights validation: origin must be a non-empty string'
- searchFlights validation error for empty destination: 'searchFlights validation: destination must be a non-empty string'
- searchFlights validation error for empty date: 'searchFlights validation: date must be a non-empty string'
- Validation runs before any network call - empty string checks use params.origin.length === 0, params.destination.length === 0, params.date.length === 0
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true' returns deterministic fixture from getMockResults(params) without calling fetch
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API values other than 'true' (unset, empty, 'false', etc.) perform real fetch call
- RapidAPI authentication header: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with this.#apiKey value
- RapidAPI host header: 'X-RapidAPI-Host' with value 'skyscanner-skyscanner-flight-search-v1.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP method is GET with headers including Accept: 'application/json'
- 4xx/5xx response rejection message: 'Skyscanner API request failed with status ${response.status} ${response.statusText || ''}'.trim()
- Network-level fetch errors (DNS, connection refused) reject with Error: 'Skyscanner network error: ${message}'
- Malformed JSON response rejects with Error: 'Skyscanner API response parse error: ${message}'
- Unexpected response shape rejects with Error: 'Skyscanner API response validation error: unexpected response shape'
- Uses global fetch API - no import of fetch from any module
- buildUrl constructs endpoint: https://skyscanner-skyscanner-flight-search-v1.p.rapidapi.com/apiservices/browseroutes/v1.0/US/USD/en-US/skyscanner-skyscanner-flight-search-v1.p.rapidapi.com/${origin}/${destination}/${date}/${adults}
- adults parameter defaults to 1 in URL when not provided or <= 0
- adults parameter uses Math.floor(params.adults) when > 0
- All parameters are URL encoded via encodeURIComponent

